  "description": "Original study: Forsythe, R., Horowitz, J. L., Savin, N. E., & Sefton, M. (1994). Fairness in simple bargaining experiments. Games and Economic Behavior, 6(3), 347-369. In the ultimatum condition a proposer offered a split of $5 and the responder accepted it, or rejected it so that both got nothing; offers were compared with dictator games. Ultimatum games appear in 47 of the 500 studies in our survey. This template has one proposer and one responder splitting $5, with no counter-offers. Participants are simulated: each is a Model participant, using the free test model until you choose a model, so the first runs only check the design; with the test model every participant takes the sample answer.",
